[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68993,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubulocystic renal cell carcinoma (TcRCC) is a rare cystic renal epithelial neoplasm with exclusive tubulocystic growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68994,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8316/3 Tubulocystic renal cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68995,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C90.0 &amp; XH7K79 Renal cell carcinoma of kidney, except renal pelvis &amp; Tubulocystic renal cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68996,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68997,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68998,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour involves the cortex and corticomedullary junction with a left predominance {19011562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68999,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are incidental findings. Haematuria, abdominal pain, and (rarely) end-stage renal disease are observed {19011562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69000,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a rare tumour, representing &lt;&nbsp;1% of renal tumours. There is a male predominance and a median age of 58.4&nbsp;years (range: 30&ndash;74&nbsp;years) {19011562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69001,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69002,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A consistent gain of chromosome&nbsp;17 and losses of chromosomes&nbsp;9 and Y are reported {26310887; 30622286}. Non-synonymous mutation in <em>ABL1</em> and <em>PDGFRA</em> were found in a few cases, whereas others have shown mutations in the chromatin-modifying genes <em>KMT2C</em> and <em>KDM5C</em> {30622286; 29056573}. Unlike in papillary renal cell carcinoma, downregulation of the microRNAs miR-155 and miR-34a has also been reported {29056573}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69003,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>TcRCC is usually well circumscribed and ranges in size from 7 to 210&nbsp;mm (median: 90&nbsp;mm). Mostly it occurs as a solitary mass, with a spongy or bubble wrap&ndash;like appearance. The cut surface consist of small white cysts containing clear fluid. No haemorrhage or necrosis is observed {23427871; 19011562; 23525677; 24375036; 27635946}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69004,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>TcRCC comprises small to intermediate-sized tubules admixed with larger cysts, which are lined by a single layer of flattened, cuboidal/columnar, and hobnail epithelium. The nuclei are enlarged and irregular, with intermediate to large and prominent nucleoli; cytoplasmic features include abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm. The stroma is often fibrotic/desmoplastic. Cases with a prominent papillary, poorly differentiated, or sarcomatoid component are probably unrelated to true TcRCC {21439613; 24375036; 27635946}. Histological grading is not necessary because nucleoli are always large {25398389}.</p>\r\n<p>Several other tumour types may show a degree of tubulocystic morphology and should be excluded. Low-grade fumarate hydratase&ndash;deficient tumours must be excluded by immunohistochemistry, but they are recognizable by their heterogeneous architecture and high-grade features {26900816}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69005,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69006,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69007,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-circumscribed tumour with small to intermediate-sized tubules and larger cysts; regular hobnail, cuboidal, or flattened cells with large nucleoli; fibrotic stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> exclusion of other tumours with tubulocystic morphology or fumarate hydratase deficiency.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69008,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging follows the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) criteria for clear cell renal cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69009,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 10,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pure TcRCC is usually an indolent tumour with a good prognosis {26310887}, with rare reports of metastasis {19011562; 31441383; 33354487}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T16:03:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]